    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d197">

                <pb facs="0330" n="296" sameAs="frus:frus1948v02/pg296"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Council/5–2648: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Embassy in France
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret   us urgent</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-05-28T14:00:00-04:00">May 28, 1948—2 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1849. Urtel 2789 and Delsec 1759 from London.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d197-f1"/> Dept will
                    wish to undertake similar approach to legislative branch US Govt by informing
                    Congressional leaders re conference recommendations before approval. US and
                    French situations not entirely analogous but possibly Bidault’s first step should envisage consultation of this kind
                    and be directed to avoidance of general debate if possible or to limitation of
                    debate to terms of conference communiqué as suggested.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d197-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>Sent Paris as 1849; repeated to London as 1959.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lovett</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d197-f1" n="1" xml:id="d197-f1-content">
                <p>Neither printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d197-f2" n="2" xml:id="d197-f2-content">
                <p>Telegram 2874, May 29, from Paris, not printed, reported that Bidault insisted that there was no way to avoid
                    a general debate in the French National Assembly but he would endeavor to limit
                    debate to the terms of the Conference communiqué (740.00119 Council/5–2948).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
